    """
    Grover-style oracle for the vertex‑cover problem on a 5‑vertex graph
    with edges (0,1), (1,4), (2,4), (3,4) and a size bound k = 3.

    The oracle marks all computational basis states |x> that correspond
    to a vertex cover of size at most 3 by applying a phase of -1.
    All ancilla qubits are returned to |0>.

    The implementation evaluates the clause f(x)=1 for the eight
    solution bit patterns (see list below) using multi‑controlled X
    gates on a single ancilla qubit.  After the phase Z is applied we
    uncompute the ancilla to restore it to |0>.
    """
